From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: let the suspend OPP floor be skipped for debugging

Add pcie_qcom.suspend_opp_floor (default Y, writable at runtime). Setting
it to N makes s2idle drop the PCIe OPP to NULL as upstream does, removing
the DDR sleep-set floor from the suspend OPP. This reproduces the s2idle
DDR-collapse hang on demand, without a rebuild, for the suspend trail
and RAM-dump debugging. The default keeps the floor.
---
diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
index ec4fc54..44d31a7 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -2197,6 +2197,12 @@ err_pm_runtime_put:
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/* Debug knob: drop the suspend OPP floor to reproduce the s2idle hang. */
+static bool suspend_opp_floor = true;
+module_param(suspend_opp_floor, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(suspend_opp_floor,
+		 "Keep the DT suspend OPP during s2idle (default: Y)");
+
 /*
  * Use the DT suspend OPP to retain the PCIe DDR/LLCC sleep-set votes
  * during s2idle. Suspend-to-RAM tears the link down and keeps dropping
@@ -2209,7 +2215,7 @@ static int qcom_pcie_set_suspend_opp(struct qcom_pcie *pcie)
 	unsigned long freq;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (pm_suspend_target_state == PM_SUSPEND_MEM)
+	if (pm_suspend_target_state == PM_SUSPEND_MEM || !suspend_opp_floor)
 		return dev_pm_opp_set_opp(dev, NULL);
 
 	freq = dev_pm_opp_get_suspend_opp_freq(dev);
